  "description": "Goat Willow (T1)- Located in the rear garden. Approximate height: 4m. Trunk diameter: approximately 500mm. Fell. a replacement tree should be planted in a convenient location of the rear garden and below are the three alternative species for consideration: Prunus sargentii (Sargent's Cherry,) Magnolia 'Heaven Scent' (Magnolia) Clerodendrum trichotomum(Glorybower) The new tree should be planted with a stem girth of between 12-14cm and at a minimum height of 2.5m.  The new tree is to be planted during the October 2026 and March 2027 planting season.\rReason for works:\rT1- Tree  proposed for removal to facilitate the construction of a modest timber outbuilding in the garden. The tree has been assessed as category U due to its  deteriorating physiological condition."
